{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_bbfe18a827e146f8bbffa68f","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 19 lines\n1: **SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES — §2 and H0–H4 only.** Apply the mechanical corrections below before commissioning; they require no further architect round. H5–H8 remain deferred. No files edited.\n2: \n3: `H` = [dao.stream.host-boundary.md](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md); source paths below are relative to `src/cljc/`.\n4: \n5: - **N1 — Substantively resolved, wording correction required:** §2.4 supplies exclusive mutation rights, transitive freeze, reader restrictions and four assigned obligations. Verified `ringbuffer.cljc:131` stores the value directly. Fresh-return wording contradicts the intended ownership transfer; see M1.\n6: - **N2 — Resolved as a design obligation:** §3.1/H0 require the committed `tools.namespace` tool, tagged outputs and independent agreement. My fresh reader-based traversal reproduced **142/140/141**, **133 shared**, including JVM `yin/repl/host.cljc`. Verified `dao.pretty` implementation and REPL display use.\n7: - **N3 — Substantively resolved:** §8.2 explicitly retains B-tree atomics/references and codec files. Verified substantive `btree.cljc:102–119,212–245` arms. Baseline/final bookkeeping needs M2–M3.\n8: - **N4 — Resolved:** §2.4, table D and H1–H3 assign `aset` return preservation, JS/Dart `acopy` prevalidation, strict UTF-8 and direct tests. Source confirms current array loops and UTF-8 library calls. Risk is revised.\n9: - **N5 — Resolved:** H0/H2/H3 specify recursive scanning, zero-files failure and distinct no-match/error statuses.\n10: - **N6 — Resolved:** §10 counts seven profile files and at least five test namespaces, matching slices. Table A independently totals **76**.\n11: \n12: | ID | Severity | File:line | Evidence | Correction |\n13: |---|---|---|---|---|\n14: | M1 | Medium | H:223 | Returning fresh storage is called publication, which immediately freezes it, despite explicitly transferring mutation rights to the caller. This would prohibit subsequent `set!`/`aset`. | Separate fresh-result ownership transfer from freezing publication. Preserve the explicitly intended caller mutation right. |\n15: | M2 | Medium | H:768 | Literal H2 grep also matches untouched `dao/data.cljc:54` documentation and out-of-scope `dao/postgraphics/lowering.cljc:587` (`rgba8unorm`). Therefore its asserted result is false. | Gate executable host references within the adopted closure; exclude comments/string false positives explicitly. Preserve scan-error handling and codec file ownership. |\n16: | M3 | Low | H:744,754,766 | “Baseline” includes seven future files; the lane-specific category can retain the Dart Jing writer that H4 deletes. | Distinguish H0 baseline from planned additions; explicitly subtract both deleted Jing writers from the final list. |\n17: | M4 | Low | H:877,887,1110 | §8.1 lists 16 existing files edited plus three deleted, not 20 edited; risk calls unchanged `aset` a behaviour change; appendix retains old closure totals. | Reconcile these counts/labels; update the stale r3 heading at line 13. |\n18: \n19: **Could not verify:** the future committed closure tool/agreement report, compiler-resolved completeness, proposed tests or three-lane execution, exhaustive caller ownership compliance, and H4 performance. These remain implementation acceptance obligations."}],"deferred":false}}
{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_bbc3f4c6aee94936880c6745","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 38 lines\n1: Created-GMT: 2026-10-20 15:10:00 GMT\n2: Created-Local: 2026-10-20 22:10:00 +07\n3: Coding-Agent: claude\n4: Model: claude-fable-5-1\n5: Session-ID: 36134bec-9cbd-4852-b78c-4901af66fd02\n6: Task: host-boundary design r5, apply astra's mechanical corrections M1-M4\n7: Role: Architect\n8: Deliverable: docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md edited in place (r5); no src edits, nothing staged.\n9: Labels: V verified by reading. No lane run. Astra's SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES covers §2 plus H0-H4 only; the M1-M4 text should be confirmed by a non-Claude reviewer before H0 is dispatched.\n10: \n11: # Rationale\n12: \n13: Each correction was verified before editing. M2 is real: a literal grep over\n14: `src/cljc` for the H2 class names matches six files, including the docstring\n15: at `dao/data.cljc:54` and the out-of-scope `dao/postgraphics/lowering.cljc`\n16: (`rgba8unorm`); the gate is now a reader-level scan of closure-tool-tagged\n17: files (§8.3), with codec files unscanned and scan errors distinct from \"no\n18: hits\". M1 splits ownership transfer (a fresh result gives the caller the\n19: exclusive mutation right) from freezing publication (append, nesting, seam\n20: handoff, content handle); the four obligations read unchanged. M3 marks the\n21: seven `dao.host.*` files as planned additions outside the H0 baseline, lists\n22: the Dart Jing writer under migration sources rather than seams, and\n23: subtracts both deleted writers from the final list. M4 reconciles the\n24: counts (16 edited, 3 deleted), drops `aset` from the behaviour changes (two,\n25: not three, in §6, §10 and §14), updates the appendix totals to 142/140/141\n26: with 133 shared, and the header to r5 with the sign-off line. Scope is\n27: unchanged; OQ7 and OQ8 stay open.\n28: \n29: Note: the document was being edited concurrently by another session while\n30: this round ran; the final text was re-read and reconciled (no duplicate\n31: paragraphs, one H3 cell).\n32: \n33: # Disposition\n34: \n35: - M1: accepted; §2.4 bullets \"Exclusive mutation right, ownership transfer, and freezing publication\" (lines 226-244).\n36: - M2: accepted; new §8.3 (lines 801-819), H2 and H3 acceptance cells (lines 714-734), §6 (lines 665-671).\n37: - M3: accepted; §8.2 intro (lines 746-753), profile and seams rows, first row, \"Baseline versus additions and deletions\" paragraph (lines 789-800).\n38: - M4: accepted; §10 cost and risk (lines 927-945), §14 (line 1113), appendix closure row, header (lines 13-21)."}],"deferred":false}}
