uses invalid sequences; never substitutes U+FFFD), `nfc` (Unicode      |     |       |\n517: |                    | 16.0) from `data.cljc:119-173`, `debruijn.cljc:241,310-321`, `jing.cljc:65-71,131-135`,              |     |       |\n518: |                    | `sign.cljc:62-66`.                                                                                   |     |       |\n519: +--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n520: | `dao.host.hash`    | P: `blake3-bytes`, `sha256-bytes` (`jing.cljc:59-135`; the string forms become portable over         | 2   | H3    |\n521: |                    | `text`).                                                                                             |     |       |\n522: +--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n523: | `dao.host.sign`    | P: `keypair-from-seed` (`sign.cljc:75-104`, seed replay), `sign`, `verify`. `generate` (fresh        | 3   | H3    |\n524: |                    | entropy, `:114-124`) stays in `yin.vm.linker.sign` until the deferred design moves it.               |     |       |\n525: +--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n526: | `dao.data.arrays`  | In place (OQ2). P: `anew` (fresh), `aget`, `alength`, `aclone` (fresh), `asub` (fresh), `aconcat`    | 12  | H2    |\n527: | (member by         | (fresh), `ainsert-at` (fresh), `aremove-at` (fresh), `from-coll` (fresh); M: `aset`, `acopy`         |     |       |\n528: | reference)         | (memmove), `asort` (stable; `parallelSort` replaced). `arrays.cljc:28-182`.                          |     |       |\n529: +--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n530: \n531: **Table B: portable over the profile, no host arm (P).** Base64 (replaces\n532: `goog.crypt.base64`, `dart:convert`, the JVM codec; **a replacement, not code\n533: motion**; oracle V `test/dao/stream/base64_test.cljc`, 3 deftests:\n534: `rfc-4648-round-trips`, `decode-is-total-and-strict`, `every-length-round-trips`);\n535: the Jing CBOR writer (replaces Boring and the Dart `cbor` package on the\n536: content path only, OQ4; a replacement; oracle table D); hex; `chunks/split`,\n537: `chunks/absorb`.\n538: \n539: **Table C: runtime prerequisites (documented and verified by existing\n540: suites; not profile entries; not a boundary).**\n541: \n542: +----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n543: | Prerequisite                     | Where, and the law a port must meet (V)                                                        | Slice   |\n544: +==================================+================================================================================================+=========+\n545: | `deftype` with per-host          | `values.cljc:39-119`: `Closure`/`Continuation` equal iff owner and payload equal; hash of      | H1 docs |\n546: | equality, hashing and printing   | `[:tag owner payload]`; print the marker text. `cbor.cljc:342-460`: `Float64` equal by bits    |         |\n547: |                                  | with NaN equal to NaN (`:365-367`); `Rational`, `Decimal` equal by fields; hashes at           |         |\n548: |                                  | `:372-444`.                                                                                    |         |\n549: +----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n550: | Atomic flag                      | `btree.cljc:87-119`: transient ownership token readable across threads.                        | none    |\n551: +----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n552: | Weak and soft references         | `btree.cljc:182-245`; default `:soft` on the JVM, `:strong` on JS and Dart (`:39-44`). A host  | none    |\n553: |                                  | without them declares `:strong`; correctness is unchanged, retention differs.                  |         |\n554: +----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n555: | `locking`, atoms, volatiles      | Five `locking` sites (§3.1); single-owner discipline elsewhere.                                | none    |\n556: +----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n557: | Host promise type                | `btree/storage.cljc:218-227`: deferred (§9.1).                                                 | defer   |\n558: +----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n559: | Dialect syntax                   | §3.3.                                                                                          | H0      |\n560: +----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n561: \n562: Layering: `dao.host.*` requires nothing in the repo; `dao` never requires\n563: `yin`. Consumers after H2: `dao.jing`, `dao.jing.cbor`, `yin.vm.integer`,\n564: `yin.vm.data`, `yin.vm.values`, `yin.vm.engine`, `yin.vm`, `yin.vm.debruijn`,\n565: `yin.vm.debruijn-code`, `dao.stream.chunks`, `dao.jing.dht`, `yin.vm.linker`,\n566: `yin.vm.linker.sign`, `dao.stream.datagram`, `dao.stream.base64`, and the\n567: three Python integer tests.\n568: \n569: ### 4.3 Oracle coverage matrix (table D)\