ations enforceable within H0–H4\" on lines 245–260. They mention the freeze rule audit and so on. Reads fine.\n\nAlso M1: check that there's no residual contradiction in §2.4: lines 219–225, the aliasing item says \"what the rule below promises about copying is nothing else\" — \"the rule below\" = the ownership item. No problem. Lines 234–236: \"Returning fresh storage is not publication.\" Good.\n\nCheck header claim: \"The four mechanical fixes M1–M4 required for sign-off were applied in r5 ... should be confirmed by a non-Claude reviewer before H0 is dispatched.\" Accurate.\n\nPotential problem: line 33 says \"**r4** answers N1–N6 within the unchanged scope,\" but the lineage makes no mention of r4 review sign-off (the astra r4 review is the SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES one, referenced on lines 14–16). The lineage lists r1 review, r2 review, r3 review, then \"r4 answers N1–N6\" — the r4 review (1792508286000) is cited in the Review status line. Minor: the lineage doesn't include the r4 review file, but the review-status block does. OK.\n\nAlso check: does §8.3 say the gate is part of H0's gate-test while H0's acceptance doesn't mention it? H0 row: \"(b) gate test `dao.host.gate-test` against the closure with List 1 ... and List 2...\" — no mention of library mode. Lines 668–669 of §6: \"scans recursively and treats a read of zero files as a failure distinct from zero matches, same for library mode (§8.3) for the H2 and H3 host-library gates.\" So library mode is mentioned in §6 and §8.3, but H0's deliverables/acceptance don't include building or testing library mode. Low-importance gap: library mode has no acceptance at H0, and its first test is at H2. Worth flagging as low importance.\n\nAlso check H3 gate: \"Ed25519 names are outside yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc (generate).\" §8.3 says the same. Consistent.\n\nNext, section ordering: 8.2 (line 745), 8.3 (line 804), 8.1 (line 824). Clearly out of order — a defect from the r5 edits (fable inserted §8.3 between §8.2 and §8.1). References: line 60 \"(§8.1)\", line 111, line 354, line 404, etc. — references are still valid but the order is wrong. Importance: low (cosmetic ordering issue) but a real defect — the task asks to check for duplicated/contradictory headings and section numbers; this is a numbering-order anomaly.\n\nAlso check whether §8 has an introduction but no \"### 8.1\"? §8 starts with \"## 8. Slices H0–H4\" and the table, then \"### 8.2\". So the first subsection to appear is 8.2. Definitely a defect.\n\nAlright, let me run the mechanical checks: em-dashes, line lengths, table border alignment, duplicate headings.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The document reads clean at first pass. Now running mechanical checks: em-dashes, line lengths, table border alignment, duplicate headings, and verifying the two false-positive sites §8.3 claims.\n\n"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_8d7458f509834a74beda207f","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"—|–","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md","output_mode":"content"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_0185006f88e849a8aafdbb67","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^#{1,3} ","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md","output_mode":"content","head_limit":80}}]}}
{"type":"event","event":{"type":"message_update","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Okay, let me verify each of the M1–M4 items and do a consistency check.\n\nM1: Lines 226–244 of §2.4: \"Exclusive mutation right, ownership transfer, and freezing publication\" — present. Ownership transfer is separated from freezing publication: yes, two sub-items. \"Returning fresh storage is not publication\" — present. The four enforceable obligations (i)–(iv) on lines 245–260 read correctly. Check: yes, (i)–(iv) are present, and consistent with the reference to (i)–(iv) in §14 (line 1107). M1 applied.\n\nM2: §8.3 lines 804–822: The host-library gate is at the reader level, not a literal grep; explicitly mentions the false positives at dao/data.cljc:54 and postgraphics/lowering.cljc:587; handles scan errors; codec-track files are excluded from the scan. The H2 gate (lines 720–724) references §8.3 \"no executable references.\" The H3 gate (lines 729–734) also references §8.3. §6 (lines 665–671) mentions library mode. Internal soundness: the gate \"takes a tagged file list from the H0 closure tool\" — closure-tagged files; reads each file with the per-lane-feature Clojure reader. Hmm — potential problem: `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` is a .cljd file, but can it be read with the Clojure reader? .cljd files might contain Dart-specific syntax that the Clojure reader can't read? In practice, ClojureDart files are usually mostly readable by the Clojure reader, but not always. Also, the gate is a test within the H0 gate (`dao.host.gate-test` run in library mode) — but the H2/H3 host-library gate runs against the adopted closure; codec files \"remain on List 1 and this mode doesn't scan them.\" Wait — but codec-track files: `dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc` and the like — are these part of the adopted closure from yin.repl.main? The lane-specific list in §3.1 includes `cljc/dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc` in the closure. If it's in the closure and not scanned, then the Boring transport writer could hold references to BigInteger, and the gate wouldn't see it — that's the design intent (codec-track files are excluded). No problem.\n\nChecking internal soundness: the H2 gate list includes `unorm` — the NFC library. But wait, §8.3 states the hit names include `java.text` — that's a namespace prefix, and symbol matching against `java.text` — reader-level symbols like `java.text.Normalizer`. Matching \"symbols that name ... `java.text`\" — probably prefix matching. This is design-level talk; no problem.\n\nAnother soundness check: the gate reads \"per-lane-feature\" files — .cljd files with the `:cljd` reader feature. Plausible.\n\nPotential defect: §8.3 says the gate is \"library mode of `dao.host.gate-test` (H0)\" — but the H0 slice table (lines 690–698) describes gate-test with List 1, List 2, and negative tests; it doesn't mention library mode / host-library scanning as part of H0 deliverables. §6 says \"same for library mode (§8.3) for the H2 and H3 host-library gates.\" Minor: the H0 acceptance criteria don't include tests for library mode. Is this a defect? The H2/H3 acceptance cells do invoke it. H0 builds gate-test; library mode is used at H2/H3, but built when...? §8.3 says \"library mode of `dao.host.gate-test` (H0)\" — suggesting H0 supplies it. H0's acceptance doesn't test it. Minor gap, might flag as low importance.\n\nM3: §8.2 introduction (lines 751–754): the seven dao.host.* files are planned additions and not part of the H0 baseline. The first row includes the Dart Jing writer under migration sources (lines 759–761). The seams row excludes `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` (lines 777–780). The \"Baseline vs. additions and deletions\" paragraph (lines 791–802): three deletions including the Dart Jing writer are subtracted. M3 applied. Check: the deletion count \"three\" matches the three deleted items in M4 §10. Yes, line 930: \"16 existing files edited and 3 deleted.\"\n\nM4:\n- Lines 930–932: 16 existing files edited and 3 deleted