est, hash-test, conformance-test, gate-test — consistent.\n\n3. \"16 edited + 3 deleted\": §10 line 930. The H0-H4 source list in §8.1 has 19 existing files (excluding the new dao/host/*): integer/host.cljc, cbor.cljc, cbor/boring.cljc, cljd.cljd, jing.cljc, sign.cljc, debruijn.cljc, debruijn_code.cljc, data.cljc, values.cljc, vm.cljc, engine.cljc, integer.cljc, chunks.cljc, base64.cljc, dht.cljc, linker.cljc, datagram.cljc, arrays.cljc = 19. 19 − 3 deleted = 16 edited. Consistent.\n\n4. aset unchanged: §2.4 line 209 \"(V arrays.cljc:50-57, unchanged)\"; §10 lines 944-946. \"two behaviour changes\" is consistent (line 670, lines 941-943). H2 acceptance criteria mention the no-partial-write test for aset — this is a test, not a change; no issue.\n\n5. Header: r5, SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES, scope narrowed to §2+H0-H4, H5-H8 unsigned. Accurate against astra's files. Also lines 18-21 mention that M1-M4 were applied in r5, pending confirmation by a non-Claude reviewer — accurate.\n\n6. OQ7/OQ8 open in §13; OQ9/OQ10 in §9.1 (lines 897-899) and line 1070. Good.\n\n7. Checking for duplicated/contradictory text from concurrent edits: headings are unique. Checking \"Baseline versus additions and deletions\" — occurs only once (line 791). Check whether §8.3 content is duplicated elsewhere: H2/H3 cells reference §8.3, no duplication. Check whether \"planned additions\" wording is duplicated: lines 752-753 and 792-794 — complementary, not contradictory.\n\n8. Remaining possible issue: HD4 (line 977) states \"H2's deletion is gated by an exact one-file grep before and an empty grep after,\" while the H2 cell (lines 714-719) now states that the pre-deletion gate uses a closure tool that reads ns forms, \"the only textual mention left is its own file.\" Also §14 lines 1085-1086: \"its gate is the one-file grep before the deletion commit and the empty grep after,\" and §10 line 950 \"the pre-deletion grep.\" These are loose \"grep\" shorthand; the formal H2 acceptance criteria is read