 as a **direct refusal** (never a substituted character); unpaired-surrogate   |     |\n611: |                                 | encode refusal; the decode cases cross-checked against the corpus `invalid-utf8` class; H1. In H3,      |     |\n612: |                                 | direct refusal tests on `dao.jing/digest-string` and `sign`'s message assembly (the consumers).         |     |\n613: +---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n614: | text: `nfc`                     | `test/yin/vm/debruijn_test.cljc` (80 deftests) example cases (V, examples only); `dao.host.text-test`:  | V+P |\n615: |                                 | a pinned subset of Unicode 16.0 `NormalizationTest.txt` (every part-1 line plus the Hangul and          |     |\n616: |                                 | composition exclusion rows); written in H1.                                                             |     |\n617: +---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n618: | hash: `blake3-bytes`,           | `test/dao/jing/hash_registry_contract_test.cljc` (15 deftests): `blake3-official-and-utf8-vector-       | V+P |\n619: | `sha256-bytes`                  | conformance`, `fixtures-load-and-agree-with-canonical-bytes`, `segment-matches-total-predicate-blake3-  |     |\n620: |                                 | and-sha256`; `test/resources/dao/jing/digest-table.edn`; `jing_test.cljc` (39 deftests) address cases.  |     |\n621: |                                 | P in H3: NIST SHA-256 short-message vectors in `dao.host.hash-test`.                                    |     |\n622: +---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n623: | sign: `keypair-from-seed`,      | `test/yin/vm/linker/sign_test.cljc` (4 deftests): `rfc-8032-vectors`, `canonical-envelope-vectors`,     | V   |\n624: | `sign`, `verify`                | `tampering-is-bad-proof`, `key-file-validation`; `sign_vectors.edn`.                                    |     |\n625: +---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n626: | arrays: all twelve              | `test/dao/data/btree_test.cljc`, `btree_transients_test.cljc`, `psset_fixtures.cljc` (V, through the    | V+P |\n627: |                                 | tree); P in H2: `asort` stability fixture (equal keys keep input order), `acopy` overlap cases, and     |     |\n628: |                                 | **no-partial-write** cases for `acopy` and `aset` with an invalid index or length on all three lanes    |     |\n629: |                                 | (the array is identical after the refusal; today JS and Dart can write first, `arrays.cljc:97-105`).    |     |\n630: +---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n631: | Jing CBOR writer (table B)      | `test/resources/dao/jing/cbor-v1.json` with `cbor-v1.errata.md` preserved; `cbor_fixtures_test.cljc`    | V   |\n632: |                                 | (14 deftests), `cbor_conformance_test.cljc` (14): byte-identical production, `documented-skips-match-   |     |\n633: |                                 | the-errata-and-leave-no-case-unrun`; `cbor_test.cljc`; `jing_test.cljc`; `file_test.cljc` (17) replay.  |     |\n634: +---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n635: | base64 (table B)                | `test/dao/stream/base64_test.cljc` (3 deftests, named above).                                           | V   |\n636: +---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n637: \n638: ### 4.4 The driver\n639: \n640: Per host, outside the core: the seam values of §4.1, clock readings as data,\n641: stdin/stdout, process exit, ambient facts as data. `yin.repl.main` is that\n642: today (V). Its deferred duties (entropy deposit, pump cadence) are §9's.\n643: \n644: ### 4.5 Relation to the conformance kit and the wasm surface\n645: \n646: `yin.vm.engine.md` §E.5 presupposes a correct host value model. H1 supplies\n647: `dao.host.conformance-test` (table D through the new namespaces); E.5.2's\n648: \"R, owner, seal, profile and manifest addresses bit-identical\" is downstream\n649: of it. The stream-implementation suite is deferred (§9.4).\n650: \n651: ## 5. What porting a host consists of (after H0-H4)\n652: \n653: 1. Implement table A (76 functions) and meet table C for the dialect; green\n654:    `dao.host.conformance-test`. Hash and signature bind a library compiled\n655:    into the same instance.\n656: 2. Load the adopted closure with a reader feature only where §3.3 syntax\n657:    requires it; the H0 gate proves zero source edits outside `dao.host.*`\n658:    and the §9 deferred files.\n659: 3. The deferred seams (§9) remain per-host work until their design lands;\n660:    until then a port supplies them as today's hosts do, by reader arms in\n661:    the deferred files, which H0's allowlist permits.\n662: \n663: ## 6. Verifiability\n664: \n665: Byte-level oracles exist for every hot primitive (table D). H0's gate has\n666: two lists (files permitted non-exempt arms, §8.2; resolved effect calls\n667: permitted) and two negative tests; it scans recursively and treats reading\n668: zero files as a failure distinct from zero matches, as does its library\n669: mode (§8.3) for the H2 and H3 host-library gates. Every H1-H4 acceptance is\n670: byte-identical against a named corpus with errata preserved; the two\n671: behaviour changes (§10) each have a direct test.\n672: \n673: ## 7. Consequence for wasm\n674: \n675: Primitives execute in-instance. The import module `dao.stream` has exactly\n676: the seven names of `dao.stream.wasm.md:38-46` (V); a primitive import is a\n677: boundary crossing and a violation of §2.2 whatever its purity. The gate that\n678: asserts a binary's import list is part of the deferred conformance suite\n679: (§9.4); until then the rule is stated here and checked by review.\n680: \n681: ## 8. Slices H0-H4 (commissionable)\n682: \n683: Expand, migrate, contract. Each slice lands alone under the quick tier on\n684: three lanes with recorded test and assertion counts; \"unchanged\" means equal\n685: counts plus any added test named. The slow tier runs once after H4.\n686: \n687: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n688: | Slice | Phase  | Change                                                                         | Falsifiable acceptance                                            |\n689: +=======+========+================================================================================+===================================================================+\n690: | H0    | freeze | No `src/` change. (a) `dev/host_boundary/closure.clj` (over                    | Gate passes on the current tree; the committed closure output     |\n691: |       |        | `clojure.tools.namespace` parsing) and its output                              | lists exactly 142/140/141 files (§3.1) and the slice report       |\n692: |       |        | `docs/design/host-boundary/closure-{clj,cljs,cljd}.edn`, each file tagged with | records agreement with an independent traversal; the gate fails   |\n693: |       |        | its §3.1 class; (b) the gate test `dao.host.gate-test` over the closure with   | on one injected `#?(:clj` in a file outside list 1 and on one     |\n694: |       |        | **list 1** (files permitted non-exempt host arms, §8.2) and **list 2**         | injected `(random-uuid)` outside list 2 (two negative tests), and |\n695: |       |        | (resolved effect calls permitted: the §3.2 sites, plus the callers of M        | fails distinctly when it reads zero files (scan failure is not    |\n696: |       |        | entries named in §2.4), exempting §3.3 patterns; the gate scans files          | zero matches). Counts recorded.                                   |\n697: |       |        | recursively and fails if it read none; (c) per-lane counts; (d) the corpus     |                                                                   |\n698: |       |        | hash set.                                                                      |                                                                   |\n699: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n700: | H1    | expand | Create `dao.host.integer`, `.float`, `.number`, `.bytes`, `.text` with today's | Green; counts unchanged plus the named new tests; the new tests   |\n701: |       |        | arms moved verbatim where the law is today's behaviour, and **with the new     | require and call `dao.host.*` directly; corpus bytes identical;   |\n702: |       |        | laws where it is not**: `utf8-encode` refuses an unpaired surrogate (today's   | the P-entry argument-immutability property test and the M-entry   |\n703: |       |        | helpers substitute: JVM `getBytes` emits `?`, `goog.crypt` and `dart:convert`  | prevalidation test pass on three lanes; `utf8-encode` direct      |\n704: |       |        | emit U+FFFD, `jing.cljc:66,69,71,132-135`, `sign.cljc:62-66`, R for the        | refusal test and `utf8-decode` strict tests pass. List 1 grows by |\n705: |       |        | library behaviour); `utf8-decode` is extracted from the already strict         | five files.                                                       |\n706: |       |        | `cbor.cljc:1240-1271` (V). The `Float64`/`Rational`/`Decimal` deftypes move    |                                                                   |\n707: |       |        | with their protocol blocks. Tests: `dao.host.conformance-test`,                |                                                                   |\n708: |       |        | `dao.host.bytes-test`, `dao.host.text-test` (table D). Table C laws written    |                                                                   |\n709: |       |        | into the docstrings of `values.cljc` and the moved carriers. No consumer       |                                                                   |\n710: |       |        | changes, so no behaviour change is observable yet.                             |                                                                   |\n711: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n712: | H2    | migr.  | Every consumer moves: `yin/vm.cljc:32`, `yin/vm/engine.cljc:38`,               | Green; counts unchanged plus the `asort` stability, `acopy`       |\n713: |       |        | `yin/vm/values.cljc:30`, `yin/vm/data.cljc:41`, `yin/vm/integer.cljc:101`,     | overlap and `acopy`/`aset` **no-partial-write** tests; corpus     |\n714: |       |        | `test/yang/python/antlr/{int_heap,int_literal,int_ops}_test.cljc` (V);         | identical. **Pre-deletion gate**: the H0 closure tool, reading    |\n715: |       |        | `dao.jing.cbor` drops `:106-254`, `:342-460`, `:483-632` for `dao.host.*`;     | `ns` forms (not text), reports `yin.vm.integer.host` required by  |\n716: |       |        | `debruijn_code.cljc:232-242,315`, `debruijn.cljc:167,241,310-321,855-885`,     | no file in `src` or `test`; the only textual mention left is its  |\n717: |       |   