n | lanes; a direct test that `digest-string` and `message` refuse an |\n729: |       |        | unpaired surrogate (refusal instead of a substituted byte), recorded in the    | unpaired-surrogate string; **host-library gate (§8.3)**: within   |\n730: |       |        | slice report; such strings are already refused by the canonical codec (corpus  | the adopted closure, no executable reference to `MessageDigest`,  |\n731: |       |        | `unpaired-surrogate` class), so no persisted address changes. Base64 made      | `Blake3`, `noble`, `blake3_dart`, `package:crypto`,               |\n732: |       |        | portable (table B; a replacement).                                             | `ed25519_edwards`, `goog.crypt.base64` outside `dao/host/`, and   |\n733: |       |        |                                                                                | for the Ed25519 names outside `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`           |\n734: |       |        |                                                                                | (`generate`); scan errors reported distinctly.                    |\n735: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n736: | H4    | migr.  | Portable Jing CBOR writer over `dao.host.*`; `dao.jing.cbor.boring` and        | Green; `cbor-v1.json` byte-identical on three lanes with the      |\n737: |       |        | `dao.jing.cbor.cljd` deleted; Boring stays for `dao.stream.cbor.boring` and    | errata skips unchanged (`documented-skips-match-the-errata-and-   |\n738: |       |        | the Dart `cbor` package for `dao.stream.cbor.cljd` (OQ4). A measurement:       | leave-no-case-unrun`); fixtures, DHT and linker image goldens     |\n739: |       |        | corpus and one large module image, old writer against new, JVM and Node.       | unchanged; the measurement in the slice report, no threshold      |\n740: |       |        |                                                                                | (OQ7). Slow tier once after landing.                              |\n741: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n742: \n743: Dependencies: H0, H1, H2 in order; H3 and H4 after H2, in either order.\n744: \n745: ### 8.2 List 1: the files permitted non-exempt host arms, baseline and final\n746: \n747: The gate never promises \"no arms across `src/cljc`\", only \"no non-exempt\n748: arms outside list 1\". List 1 is generated at H0 by the gate from the actual\n749: closure (every closure file holding a non-exempt arm, §3.3) and must equal\n750: the **H0 baseline** below, by category, with each file's reason; a\n751: difference either way is an H0 finding to resolve before H1. The baseline\n752: is today's tree: the seven `dao.host.*` files are **planned additions**\n753: (five in H1, two in H3) and are not part of the H0 baseline; they are\n754: marked as such in the table.\n755: \n756: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n757: | Category (reason)          | Files (V, from §1 and the closure)                                                              | After H4                    |\n758: +============================+=================================================================================================+=============================+\n759: | H1-H4 migration sources    | `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`,                  | Removed from list 1 as each |\n760: |                            | `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` (the Dart Jing writer; a lane-specific file counted here,    | slice lands; `sign.cljc`    |\n761: |                            | not under seams), `dao/jing.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn.cljc`,           | stays for `generate` only;  |\n762: |                            | `yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc`, `yin/vm/data.cljc`, `yin/vm/values.cljc` (table C blocks stay, as  | three of these files are    |\n763: |                            | exempt protocol syntax), `dao/stream/chunks.cljc`, `dao/stream/base64.cljc`,                    | deleted (§8.2 paragraph).   |\n764: |                            | `dao/jing/dht.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker.cljc`, `dao/stream/datagram.cljc` (bytes arms only).        |                             |\n765: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n766: | Profile (the arms belong   | Baseline: `dao/data/arrays.cljc`. Planned additions, not in the H0 baseline:                    | Stay; the seven additions   |\n767: | here by design)            | `dao/host/{integer,float,number,bytes,text,hash,sign}.cljc` (P; five join list 1 at H1, two at  | are on list 1 from the      |\n768: |                            | H3).                                                                                            | slice that creates them.    |\n769: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n770: | Retained runtime           | `dao/data/btree.cljc` (atomic flag `:102-119`, weak and soft references `:212-245`: substantive | Stay, with the table C      |\n771: | prerequisites (table C)    | arms, not protocol syntax, retained by design); `dao/data/btree/storage.cljc` (promise facade,  | reason recorded in the      |\n772: |                            | deferred §9.1); `dao/pretty.cljc` (`StringWriter`/pprint, display only, §3.1).                  | gate's list.                |\n773: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n774: | Codec-track files          | `dao/stream/ws.cljc`, `transit.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`, `cbor/boring.cljc`, `codec.cljc`,            | Stay; owned by that track;  |\n775: | (untouched by this track)  | `remote_channel.cljc`, `ws_project.cljc`, `jing/stream.cljc`.                                   | `codec.cljc:45` after C4.   |\n776: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n777: | Seams and driver           | `src/clj`, `src/cljs`, `src/cljd` seam and shadow files (§3.1 lane-specific list) **except**    | Stay, except the Dart Jing  |\n778: |                            | `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`, which is a Jing writer H4 deletes, not a seam; it is on the | writer, deleted in H4.      |\n779: |                            | baseline under the first row's `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc` twin. `yin/repl/main.cljc`,          |                             |\n780: |                            | `yin/repl/host.cljc`, `yin/repl/state.cljc`.                                                    |                             |\n781: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n782: | Deferred-scope files (§9)  | `dao/jing/file.cljc`, `dao/space/store/fs.cljc`, `dao/space/store.cljc`,                        | Stay until the deferred     |\n783: |                            | `dao/stream/journal/file.cljc`, `dao/jing/content/async.cljc`, `dao/jing/coordinate.cljc`,      | design lands.               |\n784: |                            | `dao/space/dht.cljc`, `yin/repl.cljc`, `yang/python/antlr/parser.cljc` and the other            |                             |\n785: |                            | `yang/python/antlr/*.cljc` with arms, `dao/stream/udp.cljc`, `dao/stream/journal.cljc`          |                             |\n786: |                            | (`locking`), `dao/space/transactor.cljc`, `dao/space/schema.cljc`, `yin/vm/ucf/authority.cljc`  |                             |\n787: |                            | (`locking`), and every remaining closure file whose arms are only `catch`/hint/protocol syntax  |                             |\n788: |                            | is **not** on list 1 (it is exempt by pattern).                                                 |                             |\n789: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n790: \n791: **Baseline versus additions and deletions.** The H0 baseline is the set of\n792: **existing** files above (every entry except the planned additions named\n793: in the profile row). The planned additions are the seven `dao/host/*.cljc`\n794: files (five in H1, two in H3), which join list 1 when their slices land. The deletions are\n795: three: `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc` (H2), `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc` (H4, the\n796: JVM/JS Boring wrapper) and `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` (H4, the Dart\n797: Jing writer, a lane-specific file that the seams row excludes and the first\n798: row lists, so that the lane-specific category cannot silently retain it).\n799: The final list 1 after H4 is therefore: the baseline minus the first row\n800: (except `sign.cljc` for `generate`), both deleted Jing writers included in\n801: that subtraction, plus the seven profile files. The host-library gate of\n802: §8.3 is consistent with it.\n803: \n804: ### 8.3 The host-library gate (H2, H3): executable references within the closure\n805: \n806: A literal `grep` over `src/cljc` is **not** the gate: it matches a docstring\n807: in the untouched `dao/data.cljc:54` (\"a BigInt/BigDecimal\", V) and the\n808: out-of-scope `dao/postgraphics/lowering.cljc:587` (`:rgba8unorm`, V), so\n809: its asserted result would be false. The gate is instead `dao.host.gate-test`\n810: (H0) run in library mode: it takes the H0 closure tool's tagged file list\n811: for the adopted closure (so out-of-scope files never count), reads each\n812: file with the Clojure reader per lane feature (so comments and string\n813: literals, docstrings included, never count), and collects symbols, class\n814: names and import/require forms; a hit is any such symbol naming\n815: `BigInteger`, `BigDecimal`, `clojure.lang.Ratio`, `java.text`, `unorm`\n816: (H2) or `MessageDigest`, `Blake3`, `noble`, `blake3_dart`, `package:crypto`,\n817: `ed25519_edwards`, `goog.crypt.base64` (H3) in a file outside `dao/host/`\n818: and, for H3's Ed25519 names, outside `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc` (`generate`,\n819: deferred). Codec-track files stay on list 1 and are not scanned by this\n820: mode (their arms are the codec track's). The gate fails distinctly when the\n821: closure list is empty or a file cannot be read, which is a scan error, not\n822: \"no hits\".\n823: \n824: ### 8.1 File-disjointness from the codec track, including tests (re-checked, V)\n825: \n826: Codec-track source files (`codec.md` §7.1): `dao/stream/ws.cljc`,\n827: `transit.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`, `cbor/boring.cljc`, `codec.cljc`,\n828: `remote_channel.cljc`, `jing/stream.cljc`, `data.cljc`, the four ws adapters,\n829: `yin/repl/{serve,connect}.cljc`. Codec-track test namespaces (`codec.md`\n830: §7.2): the 22 requiring Transit, including `ws_test`, `ws-codec-test`,\n831: `remote-route-test`, `loopback-net`, `transit-test`, `dao.stream.cbor-test`,\n832: `dao.jing.stream-test`, `yin.repl.main-test`.\n833: \n834: H0-H4 source files: `dao/host/*` (new), `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`,\n835: `dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`, `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`,\n836: `dao/jing.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn.cljc`,\n837: `yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc`, `yin/vm/data.cljc`, `yin/vm/values.cljc`,\n838: `yin/vm.cljc`, `yin/vm/engine.cljc`, `yin/vm/integer.cljc`,\n839: `dao/stream/chunks.cljc`, `dao/stream/base64.cljc`, `dao/jing/dht.cljc`,\n840: `yin/vm/linker.cljc`, `dao/stream/datagram.cljc`, `dao/data/arrays.cljc`.\n841: H0-H4 test files: `dao/host/*_test` (new), `yin/vm/integer_test`,\n842: `yang/python/antlr/{int_heap,int_literal,int_ops}_test`, `dao/jing/cbor_*`,\n843: `dao/jing_test`, `yin/vm/linker/sign_test`, `dao/stream/base64_test`,\n844: `yin/vm/debruijn_code_test`, `yin/vm/data_test`, `dao/data/btree_*`.\n845: \n846: Intersection: none, with two recorded deferrals: `dao/stream/codec.cljc:45`\n847: (`host-bytes?` over `dao.host.bytes`) after C4, and `dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc`\n848: (the transport writer) is **not** touched by H4. The `dao.stream.cbor-test`\n849: and `dao.jing.cbor_test` namespaces are distinct files. The deferred H5\n850: (§9.1) would touch `ws.cljc:122`, `ws_test.cljc:11` and\n851: `remote_route_test.cljc:24` (V: identity-less ring creation), which is why\n852: it is deferred behind the codec track as well as behind its own design.\n853: \n854: Coordination with a host-lane probe track: its \"narrow source adaptations\"\n855: (R: the spike touched `integer/host.cljc`, `jing.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`,\n856: `cbor/boring.cljc`) are exactly the H1-H4 files; under OQ3 that work is\n857: paused until H4 lands and needs file-level coordination, not just a rebase.\n858: \n859: ## 9. DEFERRED scope (not commissionable under this document)\n860: \n861: The following keep their design intent from r2 but are **not commissionable\n862: here**. They belong to a separate design, proposed name\n863: `docs/design/dao.stream.host-effects.md`, with its own non-Claude review.\n864: Nothing below is decided; the \"required inputs\" are the findings a\n865: successor must answer before slices exist. Slice ids H5-H8 are reserved so\n866: no other document's citation moves.\n867: \n868: ### 9.1 Entropy, identities, scheduling, ambient facts, printing (reserved H5)\n869: \n870: Intent: entropy as data the driver deposits (events in); identities derived\n871: from drawn bytes and carried in creation specs; the driver owns pumping and\n872: wake-up; ambient facts and the one core `println` as data; `gensym` with\n873: hygienic naming. Required inputs (from the r2 review R2, R6 and §3.2):\n874: \n875: - exclusive allocation and resumable consumption of an entropy stream, given\n876:   that cursors are non-destructive (`dao/stream.cljc:159-173`) and\n877:   independent readers could reuse bytes; partial batches and loss; blocked\n878:   resumption;\n879: - bootstrap identities: the entropy stream itself needs an identity before\n880:   any byte is drawn;\n881: - preserved UUID spelling: `ucf/custody.cljc:50-56` requires the\n882:   8-4-4-4-12 lowercase form, so a derived id must keep that grammar;\n883: - DHT initialization draws several values synchronously\n884:   (`space/dht.cljc:255-269`, R): failure and continuation behaviour;\n885: - async completions emitted as data: moving consumer callbacks into a\n886:   `step!` does not remove them (R2); the `btree.storage` promise facade and\n887:   `content.async` consumers need a data-shaped completion;\n888: - the JVM blocking content driver selected at `coordinate.cljc:80`\n889:   (`driver.clj:169-206`: clock and sleep) is lane-specific IO inside a\n890:   portable composition and needs its own disposition;\n891: - the codec-track test edits `ws_test.cljc:11` and `remote_route_test.cljc:24`\n892:   and the `ws.cljc:122` site: staged compatibility or an explicit dependency\n893:   on C4; a re-estimate of the slice (the r2 estimate of about twenty files\n894:   was understated: UCF custody and holder migrations are included);\n895: - `gensym` hygiene: compiler counters need hygienic naming, not a reset;\n896:   `transact.cljc:35` tempids need separate treatment;\n897: - OQ9 (entropy shape: stream versus identity-in-spec with driver-minted\n898:   secrets; both avoid core generators, the r2 recommendation overclaimed)\n899:   and OQ10 (compiler `gensym`) move to that design.\n900: \n901: ### 9.2 The durable-storage seam (reserved H6)\n902: \n903: Intent: one seam beneath the journal with enumerated lower operations; the\n904: claim-file algorithm portable; capability map (`lock-kind`,\n905: `directory-sync?`, `failure-model`). Required inputs (R5, A7): the atomic\n906: replacement at `store/fs.cljc:352-387` renames **before** the directory\n907: sync (`:364-370`, `:382-383`, V), so a sync failure can leave the new HEAD\n908: visible; the seam must distinguish pre-rename failure (target unchanged),\n909: post-rename visibility (new HEAD visible, durability uncertain) and sync\n910: uncertainty, and test post-rename failure explicitly; short reads, partial\n911: appends, acquisition outcomes (`held`/`refused`/`unsupported`), durability\n912: outcomes per the declared failure model; `own-pid`, `process-alive?`,\n913: `create-exclusive!`, `unlink!`, `canonical-path` for the claim-file lock.\n914: \n915: ### 9.3 The parser stage (reserved H7)\n916: \n917: Intent: the grammar profile plus host walk as one seam value; a\n918: remote-stage test. Required input: the one `println` at\n919: `yang/python/antlr/repl.cljc:71` becomes an emitted value.\n920: \n921: ### 9.4 Stream-implementation conformance and the wasm import gate (reserved H8)\n922: \n923: Intent: the contract's outcome tables through a scripted seam against every\n924: implementation; a gate asserting a wasm binary's import list against the\n925: seven names. Required input: which implementations declare which outcome\n926: subset (`dao.stream.md`, Surfaces).\n927: \n928: ## 10. Cost and what would reverse this (H0-H4)\n929: \n930: Cost (P, from §1 and §8.1): **16 existing files edited** and **3 deleted**\n931: (`yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`,\n932: `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`), **7** `dao.host.*` files added (five in\n933: H1, two in H3); **at least 5** test namespaces added (`gate-test` in H0,\n934: `conformance-test`, `bytes-test`, `text-test` in H1, `hash-test` in H3),\n935: the 3 Python integer tests and `integer_test` re-pointed; about 10^3 tests\n936: rerun per lane (R: JVM quick tier about 4,000); about 10^1 rewritten.\n937: Base64 and the Jing writer are replacements, not code motion, and are\n938: accepted only by their byte oracles. No performance figure is claimed; H4\n939: measures.\n940: \n941: Risk, revised (review N4): the laws of §2.4 and table A are **not verbatim\n942: extraction** in two places, and each is a behaviour change with a direct\n943: test: `acopy` prevalidation on JS and Dart (H2) and strict `utf8-encode`\n944: refusal where today's helpers substitute (H1 law, H3 consumers). The `aset`\n945: return value is kept as Clojure's: unchanged, stated only so the law cannot\n946: be read as changing it. H1 medium: new namespaces plus two new laws and\n947: their property tests.\n948: H2 medium: nine consumers, the Jing carrier move, the arrays prevalidation\n949: change and the M-caller audit in one slice; mitigated by the corpus, the\n950: pre-deletion grep and splitting the slice per namespace if the report\n951: shows drift. H3 low-to-medium: the UTF-8 behaviour change is observable only\n952: on unpaired-surrogate strings, which the codec already refuses. H4\n953: low-to-medium: the corpus decides; performance unknown until measured. The\n954: ClojureDart traps are named in §14.\n955: \n956: Reversal: an owner ruling that reader arms are the intended port mechanism;\n957: a measured H4 regression that matters (the portable writer stays as oracle\n958: and a host supplies a faster one behind the same profile); owner rejection\n959: of §12 (then §2 stands as this document's reading of the existing ABI text).\n960: \n961: ## 11. Decision record\n962: \n963: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n964: | Id   | Decision                                                                                                         | Status                       |\n965: +======+==================================================================================================================+==============================+\n966: | HD1  | The governing test: dao.stream wherever the contact can be an IO action with respect to the world (§2.1-2.3); an | Owner rule (\"test 2          |\n967: |      | internal pure, total, synchronous function, or a declared mutation of an owned argument, may be a direct call.   | governs\"); r3 wording needs  |\n968: |      |                                                                                                                  | non-Claude sign-off          |\n969: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n970: | HD2  | Internal contacts form the primitive profile: 76 entries (§4.2 table A) with kinds P/M and the §2.4 ownership    | Architect r3; needs sign-off |\n971: |      | laws, plus runtime prerequisites (table C); in-instance for wasm (§7).                                           |                              |\n972: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n973: | HD3  | Commissionable scope is §2 plus H0-H4; entropy, scheduling, storage, parser stage and stream conformance are     | Owner, 2026-10-20 (\"yes,     |\n974: |      | deferred to a separate design with the §9 required inputs.                                                       | proceed with the split\")     |\n975: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n976: | HD4  | H0 gates both reader arms and resolved effect calls over the committed per-lane closure; list 1 names retained   | Architect r3                 |\n977: |      | arms; H2's deletion is gated by an exact one-file grep before and an empty grep after.                           |                              |\n978: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n979: | HD5  | H0-H4 are file-disjoint from the codec track in source and tests, with one deferred one-line edit                | Architect r3                 |\n980: |      | (`codec.cljc:45`); host-lane source adaptations in H1-H4 files are paused (OQ3) and need file-level              |                              |\n981: |      | coordination.                                                                                                    |                              |\n982: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n983: \n984: ### 11.1 Owner decisions recorded (2026-10-20)\n985: \n986: The owner adopted all six r1 recommendations: \"agree with all of fable's\n987: recommendations\"; for OQ5 separately: \"makes sense. i agree with fable's\n988: recommendation\"; for the r3 split: \"yes, proceed with the split\".\n989: \n990: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n991: | Id   | Decision as adopted                                                                                              | Status                       |\n992: +======+==================================================================================================================+==============================+\n993: | OQ1  | Scope is the `yin.repl` closure; GUI, graphics and demo namespaces excluded.                                     | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n994: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n995: | OQ2  | The profile family is `dao.host.*`; `dao.data.arrays` stays in place as a profile member by reference.           | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n996: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n997: | OQ3  | Arm-adding work in the files H1-H3 touch is paused until phase A lands; boundary-agnostic probes proceed.        | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n998: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n999: | OQ4  | Boring and the Dart `cbor` package are dropped from the Jing content path only; the transport codec keeps them.  | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n1000: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n1001: | OQ5  | Storage is a seam beneath the journal, not a streams-all-the-way-down redesign (now deferred, §9.2).             | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n1002: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n1003: | OQ6  | This track has its own orchestrator seat, independent of the codec track and any host-lane track.                | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n1004: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n1005: | Spli | Commissionable scope is the rule plus H0-H4; the rest is deferred to a separate design.                          | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n1006: | t    |                                                                                                                  |                              |\n1007: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n1008: \n1009: ## 12. OWNER PROPOSAL: amendment to datom.world.abi.md (not doctrine; not applied)\n1010: \n1011: This section is a proposal for the owner's approval (OQ8). It is **not**\n1012: verbatim doctrine and nothing in `datom.world.abi.md` or `datom.world.md`\n1013: has been edited. The owner's quoted words are marked as such; the rest is\n1014: the Architect's proposed wording, to be revised by the owner.\n1015: \n1016: **12.1 Proposed new §8 of `datom.world.abi.md`, \"The governing test\".**\n1017: \n1018: > Owner ruling, 2026-10-20 (verbatim): \"when the host boundary can be an IO\n1019: > monad then dao.stream is used. If it cannot be a monad than dao.stream\n1020: > doesnt have to be used\"; and, asked whether same-host-ness or the\n1021: > IO-action test governs: \"yes, test 2 governs\".\n1022: >\n1023: > Proposed wording. The machine is the running instance and the runtime\n1024: > state it owns; the world is everything else. A host contact uses\n1025: > `dao.stream` when it can be an IO action with respect to the world: its\n1026: > result depends on world state; it changes world state; equal calls may\n1027: > answer differently because of the world; its answer is not available at\n1028: > return; whether it completes depends on the world; or it runs in another\n1029: > process, host or trust domain. A same-host effect (a file read, a clock\n1030: > reading, entropy) is an IO action and so a stream.\n1031: >\n1032: > A contact that is a pure, total, synchronous function of the machine's\n1033: > values, or a declared mutation of a value the caller owns, may be a direct\n1034: > call. Such contacts are enumerated in a host primitive profile with an\n1035: > oracle per entry ([dao.stream.host-boundary.md](./dao.stream.host-boundary.md)\n1036: > §4.2), execute in-instance (for wasm: compiled in, never imported), and\n1037: > add no contract to `dao.stream`. Reads of owned runtime state (a weak\n1038: > reference, an atom) are neither IO nor profile entries; they are the\n1039: > dialect's runtime prerequisites. Linking a library to compute a profile\n1040: > entry is internal linkage (§5).\n1041: >\n1042: > §7's two non-adapters are read under this test: a map of functions that\n1043: > portable application code calls to reach the world is a host service and\n1044: > is rejected; a seam a stream implementation calls privately to perform its\n1045: > own IO is that implementation's adapter and is not.\n1046: \n1047: **12.2 Proposed change to `datom.world.md:70`.**\n1048: \n1049: Today: \"A host boundary is the dao.stream abstraction boundary;\n1050: implementations do not add contracts.\"\n1051: \n1052: Proposed: \"A host boundary that can be an IO action is the dao.stream\n1053: abstraction boundary; implementations do not add contracts. A pure, total,\n1054: synchronous host function is a primitive-profile entry, not a boundary\n1055: ([datom.world.abi.md](./datom.world.abi.md) §8).\"\n1056: \n1057: ## 13. Open owner decisions\n1058: \n1059: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n1060: | Id   | Question                                                                                             | Architect's recommendation (not a decision)        |\n1061: +======+======================================================================================================+====================================================+\n1062: | OQ7  | H4's measurement: what regression, if any, is acceptable for the portable Jing writer against Boring | Accept any regression under corpus identity; set a |\n1063: |      | on the JVM and Node.                                                                                 | bound after H4's numbers exist, not before.        |\n1064: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n1065: | OQ8  | Approve the §12 proposal (the ABI's new §8 and the one-sentence change to `datom.world.md:70`).      | Approve after the owner revises the proposed       |\n1066: |      |                                                                                                      | wording; §2 stands either way as this document's   |\n1067: |      |                                                                                                      | reading.                                           |\n1068: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n1069: \n1070: OQ1-OQ6 are closed (§11.1). OQ9 and OQ10 belong to the deferred design\n1071: (§9.1).\n1072: \n1073: ## 14. For a successor orchestrator\n1074: \n1075: Decided (HD1-HD5, OQ1-OQ6, the split): the rule, the exact profile with\n1076: ownership laws, the H0-H4 sequence and gates, the deferral. Open: OQ7, OQ8;\n1077: neither blocks H0-H4.\n1078: \n1079: Start with **H0**: it changes no source; commit the closure tool\n1080: (`dev/host_boundary/closure.clj`, over `clojure.tools.namespace`), its\n1081: per-lane output under `docs/design/host-boundary/` tagged by class, and the\n1082: gate test; confirm the 142/140/141 totals against an independent traversal\n1083: and reconcile list 1 with the §8.2 baseline before H1. Then H1 (new files,\n1084: their direct tests, and the two new laws: strict `utf8-encode` and M-entry\n1085: prevalidation). H2 is the first deletion; its gate is the one-file grep\n1086: before the deletion commit and the empty grep after, and it carries the\n1087: `acopy` prevalidation change and the M-caller audit (§2.4). H3 carries the\n1088: named UTF-8 behaviour change for its two consumers. H3 and H4 in either\n1089: order; slow tier once after H4. Do not start anything in §9; a separate\n1090: design document and its own non-Claude sign-off come first.\n1091: \n1092: Lanes and gates (`docs/agents/build-n-test.md`): iterate on the JVM lane\n1093: with `bb test:sub:clj dao.jing` or `yin.vm` (G0); three-lane subsystem test\n1094: at each checkpoint (G1); `bb test:changed` across all three lanes in the\n1095: worktree before landing (G2); `bb test` on master after merge (G3). Record\n1096: per-lane counts before and after every slice. The Dart lane needs `flutter`\n1097: on PATH; a fresh worktree needs `npm ci`. ClojureDart traps for exactly this\n1098: kind of file: `:cljd` first in every mixed conditional; a tail-position\n1099: `:cljd nil` silently fails; protocol method parameters never `[_ _]`;\n1100: `(- 0.0)` is `+0.0`; multi-key `assoc` on nil misbehaves.\n1101: \n1102: Review requirement: this design and any implementation an orchestrator\n1103: derives from it under a Claude model are Claude-authored. **Sign-off on this\n1104: final text (§2 plus H0-H4) and on each slice must come from a non-Claude\n1105: architect**; a Claude reviewer may review but may not be the sole sign-off.\n1106: The reviewer checks, in order: that every entry in table A is internal and\n1107: pure or declared mutating under §2.4, with the freeze rule's enforceable\n1108: obligations (i)-(iv) each backed by a test or an audited list; that H0's\n1109: committed closure output matches 142/140/141 and list 1 matches the §8.2\n1110: baseline by category; that the two negative tests and the scan-failure test\n1111: fail as intended; that H2's grep gates hold before and after the deletion\n1112: commit and the no-partial-write tests exist; that H1-H4 acceptance is\n1113: byte-identical against the named corpus with errata preserved and the two\n1114: behaviour changes are named in slice reports; that no H0-H4 edit touches a\n1115: codec-track source or test file except the recorded `codec.cljc:45` deferral;\n1116: that nothing from §9 is started.\n1117: \n1118: ## Appendix A. Citations opened for this document (2026-10-20, read only)\n1119: \n1120: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1121: | Cite                                                         | Finding                                                                                          |\n1122: +==============================================================+==================================================================================================+\n1123: | `docs/design/datom.world.md:16-32,43-48,68-71`               | Axioms; side effects as emissions; the sentence §12.2 proposes to change.                        |\n1124: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1125: | `docs/design/datom.world.abi.md:21-24,35-44,47-52,56-64,`    | One ABI; custody; machine-internal work in-instance; the floor and internal linkage; effects     |\n1126: | `75-87,94-148`                                               | out, events in; adapter discipline; the two non-adapters.                                        |\n1127: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1128: | `docs/design/dao.stream.wasm.md:29-52`                       | Seven imports; primitives have no imports.                                                       |\n1129: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1130: | `docs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:140-180,658-780`            | Contract namespace; slice file set; the 22 test namespaces (§8.1).                               |\n1131: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1132: | `src/cljc/yin/vm/integer/host.cljc:1-298`                    | 25 public functions; \"depends on nothing\".                                                       |\n1133: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1134: | `src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc:1-101`; `yin/vm.cljc:32,929`;  | Consumers of the shim (requires and `big-carrier?` sites).                                       |\n1135: | `yin/vm/engine.cljc:38,810`; `yin/vm/values.cljc:30,196`;    |                                                                                                  |\n1136: | `yin/vm/data.cljc:41,421,547`; `test/yang/python/antlr/`     |                                                                                                  |\n1137: | `{int_heap,int_literal,int_ops}_test.cljc`                   |                                                                                                  |\n1138: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1139: | `src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:1-60,95-254,342-460,483-632,`   | Reader; big-integer helpers; carriers with equality and hash; JVM Decimal/Ratio construction and |\n1140: | `733-784,1070,1177`                                          | access; byte-ordered sorting.                                                                    |\n1141: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1142: | `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:228-245,310-317`         | Float64 little-endian hex; JVM big-integer predicate (assigned to H2).                           |\n1143: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1144: | `src/cljc/dao/data/btree.cljc:36-44,87-119,182-245`;         | Reference-mode default `:soft` on the JVM; atomic flag; weak/soft references; 12 array           |\n1145: | `src/cljc/dao/data/arrays.cljc:28-182`                       | functions.                                                                                       |\n1146: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1147: | `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc:1-130`                     | Libraries; `jvm-pair` deterministic seed replay (`:75-87`); `generate` fresh entropy             |\n1148: |                                                              | (`:114-124`).                                                                                    |\n1149: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1150: | `src/cljc/dao/jing/coordinate.cljc:63-82`;                   | JVM selection of the blocking driver; clock and sleep in the driver.                             |\n1151: | `src/clj/dao/jing/content/driver.clj:160-209`                |                                                                                                  |\n1152: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1153: | `src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc:84-261,340-387`            | Claim-file lock; atomic replace renames before directory sync (§9.2 input).                      |\n1154: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1155: | `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/custody.cljc:40-56`                     | UUID grammar for occurrence ids (§9.1 input).                                                    |\n1156: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1157: | Regex: `custody.cljc:53`, `datagram.cljc:80-130`,            | ASCII grammars; dialect semantics.                                                               |\n1158: | `jing.cljc:107-111,216-221`, `fs.cljc:105`                   |                                                                                                  |\n1159: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1160: | `test/dao/stream/ws_test.cljc:11`,                           | Identity-less ring creation in codec-track tests (§8.1, §9.1).                                   |\n1161: | `test/dao/stream/remote_route_test.cljc:24`                  |                                                                                                  |\n1162: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1163: | `src/cljc/dao/postgraphics/terminal.cljc:14`                 | The 27th `random-uuid`, out of scope.                                                            |\n1164: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1165: | Closure traversals (R), three lanes: the r3 script           | 142/140/141 files, 133 shared, by file after the r3 script's `#?@` parse defect was found; the   |\n1166: | (superseded) and the r3 reviewer's independent traversal     | lane-only members and the per-file markers of §3.1.                                              |\n1167: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1168: | `rg '^\\(deftest'` over the table D files                     | Deftest names and counts: integer 25, sign 4, base64 3, data 24, hash registry 15, cbor fixtures |\n1169: |                                                              | 14, cbor conformance 14, int contract 12, jing 39, cbor 21, file 17, debruijn 80, debruijn code  |\n1170: |                                                              | 26.                                                                                              |\n1171: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1172: | `test/resources/dao/jing/{cbor-v1.json,cbor-v1.errata.md,`   | Corpus and errata; digest table; sign vectors; integer fixtures; CPython int contract.           |\n1173: | `digest-table.edn}`; `test/yin/vm/linker/sign_vectors.edn`;  |                                                                                                  |\n1174: | `test/yin/vm/integer_v3_fixtures.cljc`;                      |                                                                                                  |\n1175: | `test/resources/yang/python/int-contract-v1.txt`             |                                                                                                  |\n1176: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1177: | `git log` (`8351e639`, `eacaed90`); `docs/orchestrator-log.` | Codec C0, C1 landed; R lane counts.                                                              |\n1178: | `md:11739,12375`                                             |                                                                                                  |\n1179: +--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+"}]}],"meta":{"source":"tool","messageId":"6efa9d48-0548-4cdb-965c-b9ea8ba1d432"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Okay, let me verify each of the M1–M4 items and do a consistency check.\n\nM1: Lines 226–244 of §2.4: \"Exclusive mutation right, ownership transfer, and freezing publication\" — present. Ownership transfer is separated from freezing publication: yes, two sub-items. \"Returning fresh storage is not publication\" — present. The four enforceable obligations (i)–(iv) on lines 245–260 read correctly. Check: yes, (i)–(iv) are present, and consistent with the reference to (i)–(iv) in §14 (line 1107). M1 applied.\n\nM2: §8.3 lines 804–822: The host-library gate is at the reader level, not a literal grep; explicitly mentions the false positives at dao/data.cljc:54 and postgraphics/lowering.cljc:587; handles scan errors; codec-track files are excluded from the scan. The H2 gate (lines 720–724) references §8.3 \"no executable references.\" The H3 gate (lines 729–734) also references §8.3. §6 (lines 665–671) mentions library mode. Internal soundness: the gate \"takes a tagged file list from the H0 closure tool\" — closure-tagged files; reads each file with the per-lane-feature Clojure reader. Hmm — potential problem: `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` is a .cljd file, but can it be read with the Clojure reader? .cljd files might contain Dart-specific syntax