al output it looked longer, as if \"The deletions are\" was appended to the same line making it around 100 chars. Whatever.\n\nHmm, wait — actually in the original read, line 794 was:\n\n\"794: files (five in H1, two in H3), which join list 1 when their slices land. The deletions are\"\n\nIn the original output I really do see it as:\n```\n794: files (five in H1, two in H3), which join list 1 when their slices land. The deletions are\n```\nFine. Under 170. Moving on.\n\nAlso confirmed: line 794 of the original output actually looked like \"files (five in H1, two in H3), which join list 1 when their slices land. The deletions are\" — the grep for 101+ character lines hit 500 lines, mostly tables. This line might be over 100 but well under 170.\n\nOne more check: duplication of H3 cell (fable mentioned \"one H3 cell\") — the H3 row appears only once in the slice table. Confirmed from the read.\n\nAlso, does §8.3 mention H2 names including `unorm`? Yes, at line 815. H2 cell line 722 enumerates the same 5 names. H3 cell lines 730-733 enumerate the same 7 names as §8.3 lines 816-817. Consistent.\n\nCheck that §6 lines 668-669 reference library mode — present.\n\nM1 detail: astra sought \"Preserve the explicitly intended caller mutation right\" — lines 234-236: caller \"may `set!`, `copy!`, `aset`, `acopy` or `asort` it.\" Good. 4 obligations (i)-(iv) intact at lines 245-257. §14 references obligations (i)-(iv) — consistent.\n\nM3 detail: astra: \"explicitly subtract both deleted Jing writers from the final list\" — lines 799-801: \"the baseline minus the first row (except sign.cljc for generate), both deleted Jing writers included in that subtraction.\" Good. And the seams row excludes the Dart writer (lines 777-779). First row includes it (lines 760-761). Good.\n\nM4 detail: appendix closure line 1165: \"142/140/141 files, 133 shared\" — good. Heading line 13 r5 — good.\n\nRemaining possible defects to record:\nD1 (Low): §8 subsection order 8.2 → 8.3 → 8.1 (lines 745/804/824). Probable residue of concurrent edits/insertions.\nD2 (Low): HD4 (line 977), §10 (line 950), §14 (lines 1085-1086) still describe H2's deletion gate as a \"grep,\" while the H2 acceptance criteria (lines 714-719) specify a closure tool that reads ns forms. Loose shorthand, but exactly the kind of wording M2 corrected for the library gate; minor staleness.\nD3 (Low): §8.3 defines the host-library gate as \"dao.host.gate-test (H0) run in library mode,\" but the H0 slice row/acceptance criteria (lines 690-698) do not include library mode construction or testing; first execution is H2. Not a contradiction but a missing acceptance hook. Hmm — is this worth recording? §6 mentions it. Record as Info/Low.\n\nAlso verifying astra's M2 requirement \"Preserve scan-error handling and codec file ownership\": §8.3 lines 819-822 — codec files stay in list 1, not scanned; scan errors distinguished. Good.\n\nWhat I could not verify: table border alignment was visually verified only from exact-text read (script blocked in plan mode) — borders appeared consistent; 142/140/141 closure counts (no lane run, needs committed tools); actual absence of executable references to the enumerated host names in the current closure (didn't run reader scan); whether all H2/H3 enumerated name lists match actual library usage sites across the tree.\n\nAlso, should I double-check that the 500 lines over 100 chars are table rows not prose? House style limit given in the task is 170, so no issue.\n\nVerdict: APPLIED WITH DEFECTS (all Low) — or \"APPLIED CLEANLY\" with minor findings? M1-M4 themselves were all applied correctly; defects are consistency-level (section order, stale grep wording, H0 library mode acceptance hook). Task verdict options: APPLIED CLEANLY / APPLIED WITH DEFECTS (list) / NOT APPLIED. Since the consistency pass found defects, I'll go with APPLIED WITH DEFECTS and enumerate the three low-severity items — none of which invalidate M1-M4.\n\nWord limit: under 500 words, final response only, header fields. Header fields like the task's? \"header fields\" — reproduce Created-GMT etc.? Probably reviewer header fields: include Coding-Agent, Model, Task, Role, Verdict. Keep compact.\n\nI'm in plan mode but — this is a read-only review task; the final response is the deliverable, no plan file needed. The prompt says plan mode should write a plan, but this task explicitly requests a review response. Given plan-mode constraints, writing a plan file is optional; the deliverable is text. I'll just respond. Actually the system says \"goal: present a well-researched plan and write to ~/.commandcode/plans/.\" But the user task is a read-only review with \"final response only.\" Writing a plan file would violate \"final response only\"? Writing to the plans directory is permitted. But the task says READ-ONLY, final response only. I'll honor the task: respond only.\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Both §8.3 false-positive cites verified: `dao/data.cljc:54` is a docstring (\"a BigInt/BigDecimal\"), `lowering.cljc:587` is `:rgba8unorm` in a keyword literal. All checks complete.\n\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-20 17:34:16 GMT\nCoding-Agent: cmd | Model: qwen/qwen3.8-max | Role: Reviewer (read-only)\nDocument: docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md (r5, 1,179 lines)\n\n**Verdict: APPLIED WITH DEFECTS** (three Low; none invalidate M1-M4)\n\n**Disposition M1-M4**\n- **M1: APPLIED.** §2.4 (lines 226-244) splits ownership transfer from freezing publication; \"Returning fresh storage is not publication\" (line 235-236); caller mutation right (`set!`/`copy!`/`aset`/`acopy`/`asort`) preserved. Obligations (i)-(iv) (lines 245-260) intact and match §14's reference.\n- **M2: APPLIED.** §8.3 (lines 804-822): reader-level scan of closure-tagged files, comments/strings/docstrings excluded by construction, both false-positive sites named (verified above), codec-track files unscanned but retained on list 1, scan error distinct from \"no hits\", empty-closure failure. H2/H3 cells (lines 720-724, 729-734) and §6 (668-669) reference §8.3 with identical name lists. Gate design is internally sound.\n- **M3: APPLIED.** Seven `dao.host.*` files marked planned additions outside the H0 baseline (lines 751-754, 766-768); Dart Jing writer moved to the first row and excluded from seams (759-761, 777-779); both writers explicitly subtracted (791-802).\n- **M4: APPLIED.** 16 edited + 3 deleted + 7 added (line 930-932; 16 = the 19 existing §8.1 files minus 3 deletions, arithmetic checks); `aset` \"unchanged\" (209, 944-946); \"two behaviour changes\" consistent (§6, §10); appendix totals 142/140/141, 133 shared (line 1165) match §3.1, H0 acceptance and §14; heading is r5 with an accurate narrowed-scope sign-off claim (13-21).\n\n**Consistency:** no duplicate headings/paragraphs, no orphaned text; 76 entries (table A column sums to 76); seven profile files (5 H1 + 2 H3); five test namespaces; no em-dashes; no lines >170 cols; OQ7/OQ8 open (§13), OQ9/OQ10 in §9.1; all §-references resolve; no TOC exists.\n\n| ID | Sev | File:line | Evidence | Correction |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| D1 | Low | H:745,804,824 | Subsection order is 8.2, 8.3, 8.1 (§8.1 follows §8.3), likely insertion fallout from the concurrent edits | Move §8.1 before §8.2 or renumber |\n| D2 | Low | H:950,977,1085-1086 | HD4, §10 and §14 still call H2's deletion gate a \"one-file grep\"/\"empty grep\" while the H2 cell (714-719) specifies the closure tool reading `ns` forms | Reword to match the reader-based gate |\n| D3 | Low | H:690-698 vs 809 | §8.3 says library mode is `dao.host.gate-test` \"(H0)\", but H0's deliverables/acceptance never build or test it; first exercise is H2 | Add library mode to H0's acceptance or state it lands with H2 |\n\n**Could not verify:** the 142/140/141 closure totals and reader-scan results (nothing executed; plan mode blocked even read-only scripts, so table border alignment was checked visually from exact-text reads and appeared consistent); that no executable reference to the H2/H3 name lists exists elsewhere in today's closure."}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1792518173312,"messageId":"a800886f-0450-48c0-8b4a-cbd5ba7ca6f7"}}],"interrupted":false,"modState":{"workspace":{"cwd":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld","platform":"darwin","branch":"master","gitStatus":"M docs/orchestrator-log.md\n M mise.toml\n M public/chp/blog/python-without-foreign-functions.blog\n?? bin/claude-cloud\n?? collab/1792412960461-engineer-jolt-yin-repl-spike.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md\n?? collab/1792412960461-engineer-jolt-yin-repl-spike.claude-opus-5-5.prompt.md\n?? collab/1792412960461-engineer-jolt-yin-repl-spike.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log\n?? collab/1792413225962-engineer-jolt-yin-repl-spike-r2.claude-opus-5-5.prompt.md\n?? collab/1792413225962-engineer-jolt-yin-repl-spike-r2.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log\n?? collab/1792421958748-architect-jolt-lane-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\n?? collab/1792421958748-architect-jolt-lane-plan.gpt-6-astra.prompt.md\n?? collab/1792421958748-architect-jolt-lane-plan.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log\n?? collab/1792422615171-architect-jolt-lane-plan-review.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\n?? collab/1792422615171-architect-jolt-lane-plan-review.claude-fable-5-1.prompt.md\n?? collab/1792422615171-architect-jolt-lane-plan-review.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log\n?? collab/1792422917994-orchestrator-handoff-jolt-lane.md\n?? collab/1792423156000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\n?? collab/1792423156000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.prompt.md\n?? collab/1792423156000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log\n?? collab/1792423926000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r3.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\n?? collab/1792423926000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r3.gpt-6-astra.prompt.md\n?? collab/1792423926000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r3.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log\n?? collab/1792424621000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r4.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\n?? collab/1792424621000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r4.gpt-6-astra.prompt.md\n?? 